    "en":  {
               "headline":  "Strong Q3 results overshadowed by data-center permit setbacks; chart still trending down",
               "summary":  "SpaceX closed at $127.79 on 20 Nov 2026, down 7.69% in one day on volume about 1.2x normal. The drop came after Arizona\u0027s attorney general asked for a delay to the 9 Dec vote on its $50B AI campus. Earlier, on 17 Nov, a Texas county voted not to hold a tax-break hearing for a $24B site. On 5 Nov the stock had already fallen as much as 11% on post-election political risk. Q3 results on 20 Oct were strong, with revenue of $14.58B (+161%). Still, the chart is in a downtrend, and a lockup covering about 798M shares ends on 8 Dec.",
