               "caution":  "The next three weeks hold several risk events: an Arizona community meeting on 3 Dec, the lockup expiry on 8 Dec (up to about 798M shares) and the Cochise County vote on 9 Dec. If price fails to hold the lower band at $127.35, there is little chart support until the $104.83 52-week low. Q3 net income also leaned on about $1.6B of non-operating gains. Quarterly capex is about seven times operating income, so the bull case depends on the AI build-out paying back.",
               "opportunity":  "If Arizona approves the campus on 9 Dec and the lockup passes without heavy selling, the two worries behind November\u0027s losses could ease. The business itself is growing quickly. Starlink revenue is up 69% and subscribers nearly doubled to 13.6M, while the AI unit is already profitable and rents compute to Google and Anthropic. Price sits on the lower band with RSI 38.5. A move back above the $139 Bollinger middle would be the first sign that sellers are running out of steam.",
